 🕵️ Detection Rules: MITRE ATT&CK T1595 - Active Scanning

## Overview

**T1595 (Active Scanning)** is a **Reconnaissance** technique where adversaries actively scan victim IP blocks, ports, and services to gather information about target infrastructure before launching attacks. This includes scanning for live hosts, open ports, running services, vulnerabilities, and network topology.

### MITRE ATT&CK Context
- **Tactic**: Reconnaissance (TA0043)
- **Primary Goal**: Gather intelligence on target networks and systems
- **Secondary Goals**: 
  - Identify active hosts and network segments
  - Discover open ports and services
  - Map network topology and infrastructure
  - Find vulnerabilities for exploitation

### Official MITRE ATT&CK v20 Sub-Techniques

According to **official MITRE ATT&CK v20**, T1595 has **only 3 sub-techniques**:

| ID | Name | Description |
|----|------|-------------|
| T1595.001 | Scan IP Blocks | Scanning victim IP blocks to gather information |
| T1595.002 | Vulnerability Scan | Scanning for vulnerabilities in host configurations |
| T1595.003 | Port Scan | Identifying open ports and services on targets |

